+# Todo Due Dates Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [x]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Add optional calendar due dates, API-computed overdue status, an API filter, and the list's `nur überfällige` checkbox for ticket #1.
+
+**Architecture:** The in-memory store validates and retains `dueDate`. The HTTP app derives `overdue` from the current UTC day on every todo response and filters those representations for GET collections. The read-only page fetches the selected collection and safely renders its date and status.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24, built-ins only, browser DOM, Playwright MCP for end-to-end checks.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-23-todo-due-date-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Node 24 built-ins only, with the existing in-memory lifetime.
+- Accept only real calendar dates with a four-digit year from 0001 through 9999.
+- The visible label must be exactly `überfällig`.
+- An open todo is overdue exactly when its due date precedes today's UTC date. Undated and completed todos are never overdue.
+- Checkbox label: `nur überfällige`; test id: `overdue-filter`.
+- No create/edit forms, sorting, reminders, styling, persistence, or new dependencies.
+- Every change starts with a failing test in `test/`; screenshots stay outside the repository.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Invalid mixed-field PATCH must leave all previous fields unchanged: Task 1 asserts the full saved todo after rejection.
+- Leap centuries and very early years must validate without JavaScript Date normalization errors: Task 1 covers 1900, 2000, 0001, and 0099.
+- UTC midnight must change both status and filter membership without a write: Task 2 advances an injected clock across midnight.
+- A client-provided `overdue` must not override the derived status: Task 2 tests POST and PATCH with that extraneous field.
+- Rapid checkbox changes must preserve the latest selection: Task 3 uses delayed browser responses to verify stale results cannot replace the current list.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store dates and validate changes atomically
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/store.mjs`; create `test/store.test.mjs`; adjust the existing exact response expectation in `test/app.test.mjs` for the added `dueDate: null`.
+
+**Interfaces:** Existing `createStore()` methods remain; saved todos gain `dueDate: string | null`. `add({ title, dueDate = null })` defaults to no date; `update(id, patch)` preserves omitted fields and accepts explicit null. No stored `overdue` field.
+
