+  ```js
+  assert.equal(store.add({ title: 'A' }).dueDate, null);
+  assert.equal(store.add({ title: 'B', dueDate: '2000-02-29' }).dueDate, '2000-02-29');
+  assert.throws(() => store.add({ title: 'C', dueDate: '1900-02-29' }), ValidationError);
+  ```
+  Include valid `0001-01-01`, `0099-12-31`, `9999-12-31`; invalid `0000-01-01`, `2026-02-29`, `2026-04-31`, empty/unpadded/timestamp strings, numbers, booleans, objects and arrays. Test date replacement/removal/preservation and mixed invalid patches (valid title with invalid date/done; invalid title with valid date), asserting the full prior todo is unchanged.
+- [x] Run `node --test test/store.test.mjs`; confirm missing date support causes assertion failures.
+- [x] Implement strict date validation in `src/store.mjs` and stage validated patch values before changing the saved todo. Use an ISO round trip plus explicit year bounds to reject normalized invalid dates.
+- [x] Update the existing response expectation for `dueDate: null`; run `npm test`, expecting all tests to pass.
+- [x] Commit store, store tests, and expectation update as `feat: validate optional todo due dates`.
+
+### Task 2: Derive overdue status and filter the API
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/app.mjs` and `test/app.test.mjs`.
+
+**Interfaces:** Extend to `createApp(store = createStore(), now = () => new Date())`; preserve all existing calls. Todo responses from POST/PATCH/GET item/GET collection add `overdue: boolean` without changing saved data. `GET /todos?overdue=true` filters the derived representations. Only exact `true` activates filtering.
+
+- [x] Add failing HTTP tests using a supplied store and mutable clock; extend the test server helper to accept an app handler. At `2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z` assert yesterday/open is true, today/future/completed/undated are false. Verify all response routes, POST/PATCH date validation returns HTTP 400, null removal and omitted-field preservation.
