+  assert.equal((await (await fetch(`${base}/todos/1`)).json()).overdue, true);
+  assert.deepEqual((await (await fetch(`${base}/todos?overdue=true`)).json()).map(t => t.id), [1]);
+  ```
+  Also test no matches, `overdue=false`, ignored unknown values, unchanged insertion order, completion/reopening, UTC midnight status/filter changes without writes, and ignored client-supplied `overdue`. Update the original exact response expectation for `overdue: false`.
+- [x] Run `node --test test/app.test.mjs`; confirm assertions fail because the derived field/filter are missing.
+- [x] Add a per-request todo presentation helper that derives the current UTC date from `now().toISOString().slice(0, 10)`, compares validated dates lexically, and adds `overdue`. Apply it to every todo response and filter the GET collection after presentation.
+- [x] Run `npm test`, expecting all tests to pass.
+- [x] Commit as `feat: expose overdue status and filter todos`.
+
+### Task 3: Display dates and add the overdue checkbox
